ATMOS FC USER-FACING CONTENT RULE

External providers and internal data plumbing may support Atmos FC behind the
scenes, but they must not be presented as product content in the interface.

- Never render provider IDs, Wikidata IDs, matching confidence, source-matching
  review states, provider names, API names, or other internal sourcing mechanics
  as user-facing labels, facts, statuses, metrics, headings, or descriptive copy.
- Provider-backed information must be translated into useful Atmos FC content.
- Source links may include relevant official or editorial references, but must
  use human-readable labels and must not expose internal identifiers or matching
  machinery.
- Only expose provider or sourcing diagnostics when Spencer explicitly requests
  a diagnostic or administrative interface.
- Never imply that Atmos FC has user profiles, personal reading history, saved
  reads, user-owned analyses, or personalised tracking unless those features
  have actually been implemented and Spencer has explicitly approved them.
- The current product language is match search and match analysis. Describe
  stored information as Atmos FC match data, never as something a user has read.
